    <briefdescription>
<para>TTL-enforced HKDF key-derivation cache interface. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="classthemis_1_1utils_1_1_i_h_k_d_f_key_cache_1a841c1b01cdf49352cfd089b783961c5d" kindref="member">derive()</ref> returns a cached key when the TTL has not expired; it evicts and re-derives when the TTL has expired, ensuring stale key material is never served. <ref refid="classthemis_1_1utils_1_1_key_handle" kindref="compound">KeyHandle</ref>&apos;s destructor zeroes key bytes on release.</para>
<para>No method on this interface exposes raw key bytes beyond <ref refid="classthemis_1_1utils_1_1_key_handle_1a2f2537db2c5e2ad514ee15356694de8b" kindref="member">KeyHandle::bytes()</ref>. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
